From: Alexandr Mironov <7062352+alexandr-mironov@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] device-xiaomi-vayu: declare the vbmeta partition

The device ships with AVB enabled. Flashing postmarketOS without writing a
vbmeta image that has the verification-disabled flag set makes the bootloader
reject the unsigned boot image: the device shows the POCO splash screen and
drops back into fastboot.

`pmbootstrap flasher flash_vbmeta` handles this, but it refuses to run because
deviceinfo does not name the partition:

    ERROR: Your device does not have 'vbmeta' partition specified;
    set 'deviceinfo_flash_fastboot_partition_vbmeta' ...

The partition is called `vbmeta` (see the partition layout on the device wiki
page). With this line, `flash_vbmeta` works and the device boots.

Tested on Xiaomi POCO X3 Pro (vayu_global, M2102J20SG), Huaxing panel.

---
 device/testing/device-xiaomi-vayu/deviceinfo | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/device/testing/device-xiaomi-vayu/deviceinfo b/device/testing/device-xiaomi-vayu/deviceinfo
index c4f4135..96d161b 100644
--- a/device/testing/device-xiaomi-vayu/deviceinfo
+++ b/device/testing/device-xiaomi-vayu/deviceinfo
@@ -29,3 +29,4 @@ deviceinfo_flash_offset_ramdisk="0x01000000"
 deviceinfo_flash_offset_second="0x00f00000"
 deviceinfo_flash_offset_tags="0x00000100"
 deviceinfo_rootfs_image_sector_size="4096"
+deviceinfo_flash_fastboot_partition_vbmeta="vbmeta"
